<article class="env-lemma" id="02I2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02I2">Lemma <span data-tag="02I2">5.11.5</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. The following are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$X$ is catenary, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$X$ has an open covering by catenary spaces. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Moreover, in this case any locally closed subspace of $X$ is catenary. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Suppose that $X$ is catenary and that $U \subset X$ is an open subset. The rule $T \mapsto \overline{T}$ defines a bijective inclusion preserving map between the closed irreducible subsets of $U$ and the closed irreducible subsets of $X$ which meet $U$. Using this the lemma easily follows. Details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>